THIS W.P. IS FILED UNDER ARTICLES 226 AND 227 OF THE CONSTITUTION OF INDIA PRAYING TO QUASH THE NOTIFICATION DATED 12.05.2004 ISSUED U/SEC 3(1) OF THE KARNATAKA INDUSTRIAL AREAS DEVELOPMENT ACT, 1966 VIDE ANNEXURE-Q; THE NOTIFICATION DATED 12.05.2004 ISSUED U/SEC 1(3) OF THE KARNATAKA INDUSTRIAL AREAS DEVELOPMENT ACT, 1966 VIDE ANNEXURE - R, THE NOTIFICATION DATED 12.05.2004 ISSUED U/SEC 28(1) OF THE KARNATAKA INDUSTRIAL AREAS DEVELOPMENT ACT, 1966 VIDE ANNEXURE - S AND THE NOTIFICATION DATED 19.10.2017 ISSUED U/SEC. 28(4) OF THE KARNATAKA INDUSTRIAL AREAS DEVELOPMENT ACT, 1966 VIDE ANNEXURE - AB TO THE WRIT PETITION, IN SO FAR AS THE SCHEDULE LANDS ARE CONCERNED;
K. Gajendran vs The State Of Karnataka on 15 March, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/70615664/
7

In this petition, petitioners have sought for the following reliefs:-
(a) Issue a writ in the nature of certiorari to quash the notification bearing No. CI 162 SPQ 04 dated 12.05.2004 issued U/Sec 3(1) of the Karnataka Industrial Areas Development Act, 1966 vide Annexure-Q, the Notification bearing No. CI 162 SPQ 04 dated 12.05.2004 issued U/Sec 1(3) of the Karnataka Industrial Areas Development Act, 1966 vide Annexure - R, the Notification bearing No. cI 162 SPQ 04 dated 12.05.2004 issued U/Sec 28(1) of the Karnataka Industrial Areas Development Act,
1966 vide Annexure - S and the Notification bearing No. CI 117 SPQ 2014 Bengaluru dated 19.10.2017 issued U/Sec 28(4) of the Karnataka Industrial Areas Development Act, 1966 vide Annexure - AB to the Writ Petition, in so far as the schedule lands are concerned;

In support of his contentions, learned Senior counsel for the petitioners has placed upon the following decisions:-
(i) State of Punjab vs Gurdial Singh - (1980)2 SCC 471;
(ii) Patasi Devi vs State of Haryana - (2012) 9 SCC 503;
(iii) Uddar Gagan Properties Limited vs Sant Singh - (2016) 11 SCC 378 (iv) K S Chandrashekar vs Special Land Acquisition Officer - ILR 1991 KAR 1314;
(v) N Rajanna vs State of Karnataka - (2010) 6 SCC 596;

In support of their contentions, they have relied upon the following decisions:-
(i) P. Rajappa vs. State of Karnataka - 2004 SCC Online Kar 197;
(ii) P. Narayanappa vs. State of Karnataka (2006)
7 SCC 578;
(iii) North Eastern Railway vs. Chhedi Lal 1987 Supp SCC 609;
(iv) Municipal Corporation, Aurangabad vs. State of Maharashtra (2015) 16 SCC 689;
